1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,320
The price printed on the yellow shelf tag is not what you pay at the register.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,180
In federal court, regulators caught discount giant dollar general quietly overcharging customers

3
00:00:08,180 --> 00:00:11,520
at checkout across thousands of stores after 30,000 complaints.

4
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:16,440
The company blamed manual tag updates, so why did millions of shoppers never say a word?

5
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:20,440
Because when you are standing at the register with four tired strangers waiting behind you,

6
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,520
you feel embarrassed to hold up the line over 35 cents.

7
00:00:23,740 --> 00:00:25,520
Retailers count on that social shame.

8
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:30,220
Nobody sews over a quarter, but when 10 million polite shoppers walk away every day,

9
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:33,260
30 cents turns into a hundred million dollar corporate dividend.

10
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:36,960
Next time that register screen jumps, do not stay quiet to be polite.

11
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,380
Hold up the line, because that extra quarter wasn't an honest mistake.

12
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,760
It was your quiet surrender.

